    "iOS has no numbered pagination control, so every platform shows the same pager: rounded hairline cells at 28, 34 or 40 (small, default, large), the page numbers in 13px mono numerals, and the current page in the accent fill with a soft glow beneath it. Previous and Next carry a chevron and a \"Prev\" / \"Next\" label beside the numbers (the chevron alone at the small size and in the compact row), the truncation gap is a quiet text ellipsis (…), and the rows-per-page trigger sits on the field edge. A resting page or arrow takes the hover wash at once; a disabled pager dims as one, and in an enabled pager the arrow at either end dims on its own.",
    "In glass mode the current page is a brand-tinted control-layer puck behind its number; the other pages and the hairline arrows paint no surface, so they stay bare. Beyond seven pages a page change also shifts the window (an ellipsis moves, a number appears or drops out). Solid mode keeps the accent fill.",
